<title>FRANCE: France reports free-market grain bids.</title>
<headline>France reports free-market grain bids.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain traders made the following bids for refunds to export free-market grain at this week's EU tender, French cereals office ONIC said. Bids are in Ecus/tonne.</p>
<p>		     --- April 3 --		--- March 20 ---</p>
<p>		  Tonnage   Range of Bids    Tonnage  Range of Bids</p>
<p> Soft wheat   290,500    4.74-14.99	1,097,500    8.73-17.99</p>
<p> Barley	 135,000   30.74-31.96	  321,000   28.77-32.49</p>
<p> Rye	    No bids				6,000   Not given</p>
<p> Durum	  No bids			  No bids</p>
<p>There was no European Union grain tender last week.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
